WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.333
Follow the DNA template.

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:04.540
RNA polymerase binds at the promoter and builds a

00:00:04.620 --> 00:00:06.600
complementary messenger RNA strand.

00:00:07.180 --> 00:00:09.598
Watch the RNA message lengthen and leave the template.

00:00:10.120 --> 00:00:10.902
This is transcription.

00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:14.891
The DNA sequence provides
the information; the RNA carries

00:00:14.900 --> 00:00:15.360
a copy.

00:00:15.920 --> 00:00:17.790
Translation comes next at a ribosome.

00:00:18.340 --> 00:00:21.780
Transfer RNA matches messenger
codons while a polypeptide is

00:00:21.820 --> 00:00:22.200
assembled.

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:25.380
Do not confuse message
production with protein assembly.
